{
  "_doc": "BOATZ ship art (top-down, bow at +x — WorldRenderer rotates the whole asset by heading = atan2(dy,dx)). Hull CLASS reads from silhouette: `sloop` (1 mast, sleek), `brig` (2 masts, standard), `galleon` (3 masts + sterncastle), and `ship` (the fallback for any unlisted type = the brig). Every part is wrapped in a `Bob` GROUP whose ambient `*` clip gives a gentle heel+bob and whose play-once `sinking` clip rolls the vessel onto her beam-ends as she founders. The SAILS are quadPath crescents that BILLOW (an animated control point) and take the runtime `color` as their fill — that dye is the ship's home-port colour for a merchant, near-black for a pirate, naval navy for a privateer — so faction + trade lane read at a glance while the hull keeps its own weathered timber colour. A parchment PENNANT streams from the mainmast and flutters. States: idle (in port, sails furled) / sailing (full sail) / docked / damaged (scorched hull + thinner sail + a plume of `damageSmoke`) / sinking (the roll clip + smoke).",

